          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A Cheng space is a version of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measurable+space"} measurable space
            developed by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Henry+Cheng"} Henry Cheng
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+mathematics"} classical mathematics
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-ideal"} ideal
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/null+subsets"} null subsets
            (or a
            = succeed "-filter" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subsets"} full subsets
          %p
            Some of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abstract+nonsense"} abstract nonsense
            below is original research (by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Toby+Bartels"} Toby Bartels
            and
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Todd+Trimble"} Todd Trimble
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#BishopBridges"} Bishop &amp; Bridges
          %h2#motivation Motivation
          %p
            From a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive
            perspective, there are a couple of related problems with the classical theory of measurable spaces. One is that the notion of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-algebra"} algebra
            is highly suspicious, because it relies on an operation,
            = succeed "ation," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complement"} complement
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intuitionistic+logic"} intuitionistic logic
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+line"} real line
            to itself, regardless of measurability, is
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous
          %p
            Indeed, if we set aside the general theory of measurable spaces and simply do Lebesgue measure ad hoc in a constructive (even predicative) way, we find that instead of measurable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
            we really want measurable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+functions"} partial functions
            whose domain of definition is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subset"} full subset
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/almost+functions"} almost functions
            %em after
            the structure of the measurable space has been given, we are at an impasse.
          %p
            There is a way out, due to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Henry+Cheng"} Henry Cheng
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+subsets"} disjoint subsets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,B)
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∪
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \cup B
            is full —with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ¬
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,\neg{A})
            being the motivating example in the classical theory—, but we let the Cheng measurability structure itself tell us which pairs those are. Once we fix a particular measure, we may find additional pairs whose union is full, somewhat like finding additional measurable sets when taking the completion in the classical theory (although taking the completion is a separate phenomenon here), but that's all right; the important thing is that each pair chosen really is full in any measure used (much as each set in a classical
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            in several steps.
          %h3#the_boolean_semialgebra_of_disjoint_pairs The Boolean semi-algebra of disjoint pairs
          %p
            A
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+subsets"} disjoint pair
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a pair
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,B)
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsets"} subsets
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            such that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersection"} intersection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∩
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \cap B
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+subset"} empty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            defines a disjoint pair
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ¬
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [A] = (A,\neg{A})
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is empty) is
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ∅
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ∅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\empty,\empty)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⇔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi C
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∧
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi B
                  %mo ⊇
                  %mi D
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,B) \subseteq (C,D) \;\Leftrightarrow\; A \subseteq C \;\wedge\; B \supseteq D .
          %p
            Similarly, we make the usual operations on sets into operations on disjoint pairs by applying formal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Morgan+duality"} de Morgan duality
            to the second component:
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ∅
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi ∅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ∅
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \empty = [\empty] = (\empty, X)
              ;
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ∅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = [X] = (X, \empty)
              ;
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∪
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,B) \cup (C,D) = (A \cup C, B \cap D)
              ;
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∩
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo ∪
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,B) \cap (C,D) = (A \cap C, B \cup D)
              ;
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋂
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bigcup_i (A_i,B_i) = (\bigcup_i A_i, \bigcap_i B_i)
              ;
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋂
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋂
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bigcap_i (A_i,B_i) = (\bigcap_i A_i, \bigcup_i B_i)
              \.
          %p
            (Note that we do not write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [A]
            as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            except when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is given as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ∅
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \empty
            or
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ∩
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [A \cap B] = [A] \cap [B]
          %p
            These operations form the disjoint pairs into a
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice"} lattice
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+lattice"} complete lattice
            and a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributive+lattice"} distributive lattice
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+set"} power set
            is, constructively, completely distributive only in one direction, making it a
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frame"} frame
          %p
            Finally, we define the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complement"} complement
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,B)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            (which usually are not even disjoint) but instead simply by reversing them:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ¬
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg(A,B) = (B,A) .
          %p
            Then an actual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Morgan+duality"} de Morgan duality
            holds for these operations:
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ¬
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋂
                      %mi i
                    %mo ¬
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg\bigcup_i (A_i,B_i) = \bigcap_i \neg(A_i,B_i)
              ;
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ¬
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋂
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                      %mi i
                    %mo ¬
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg\bigcap_i (A_i,B_i) = \bigcup_i \neg(A_i,B_i)
              ;
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ¬
                    %mo ¬
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg\neg(A,B) = (A,B)
              , the famous
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+negation"} double negation
              law.
          %p
            We can go on to define the relative complement
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∖
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,B) \setminus (C,D)
            and symmetric difference
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊎
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,B) \uplus (C,D)
            in terms of complements, intersections, and unions as usual, and they obey many of the usual classical laws. (For instance,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊎
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \uplus
            is —through a fairly lengthy calculation— associative, which is not constructively true of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+difference"} symmetric difference
            on a power set.)
          %p
            At this point, the reader could be forgiven for thinking that we have cleverly pulled a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boolean+algebra"} Boolean algebra
            out of a mere
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+algebra"} Heyting algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∪
                  %mo ¬
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∪
                  %mi B
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ∅
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,B) \cup \neg(A,B) = (A \cup B, \empty)
            (and similarly for intersection) and there is no requirement that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∪
                    %mi B
                    %mo =
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \cup B = X
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rig"} rig
            = succeed "." do
              %strong Boolean semi-algebra
          %p
            This is all a special case of the
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chu+construction"} Chu construction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Chu
                      %mi TV
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi P
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ∅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Chu_{TV}(P X, \empty)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi TV
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} TV
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriching
            category of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truth+values"} truth values
          %h3#the_semialgebra_of_complemented_pairs
            The
            = succeed "-semi-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
          %p
            Given a set
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
              \-semi-algebra
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a collection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℳ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
            of disjoint pairs in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "," do
              %strong complemented pairs
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi ∅
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ∅
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\empty] = (\empty,X)
            is a complemented pair; 2. If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,B)
            is a complemented pair, then so is its complement
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (B,A)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 3
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A_1,B_1), (A_2,B_2), (A_3,B_3), \ldots
            are complemented pairs, then so is their union
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋂
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\bigcup_i A_i, \bigcap_i B_i)
          %p
            The arguments above that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℳ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
            is closed under countable intersections, relative complements, and symmetric differences goes through. (We can also define analogous notions of semi-algebra,
            = succeed "-semi-ring," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-algebra"} algebra
          %p
            Finally, a
            %strong Cheng measurable space
            or simply a
            %strong Cheng space
            is a set equipped with a
            = succeed "-semi-algebra." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
          %p
            (Incidentally, the reason why we do not use the term ‘measurable pair’ is that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            may easily both be measurable in some sense yet without having
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,B)
            as a complemented pair. In particular,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ∅
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ∅
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\empty,\empty)
            is rarely a complemented pair —although that is not forbidden either—, yet it is hard to call it non-measurable.)
          %h3#measurable_sets_and_functions Measurable sets and functions
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            of a Cheng space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measurable+subset"} measurable
            if there is some complemented pair
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,B)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subset"} full
            if, for some complemented pair
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,B)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            contains the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/union"} union
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∪
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \cup B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/null+subset"} null
            if, for some such
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,B)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is disjoint from
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∪
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \cup B
          %p
            Given two Cheng measurable spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/almost+function"} almost function
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+function"} partial function
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            such that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain"} domain
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is full. An almost function is
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measurable+function"} measurable
            if, given any complemented pair
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,D)
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,B)
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi p
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⇔
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{p\colon X \;|\; p \in A \iff f(p) \in C\}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi p
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi B
                  %mo ⇔
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{p\colon X \;|\; p \in B \iff f(p) \in D)
            are both full.
          %p
            Two (measurable) functions are
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/almost+equal"} almost equal
            if their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equaliser"} equaliser
            is full.
          %p
            Cheng spaces, measurable almost functions between them, and almost equality between them form a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cheng
                    %mi Sp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cheng Sp
          %h2#completion Completion
          %p
            A Cheng space is
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+measure+space"} complete
            if, whenever
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,B)
            is a complemented pair and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⇔
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \Leftrightarrow C
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo ⇔
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \Leftrightarrow D
            are full, then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,D)
            is a complemented pair. In particular, every full set and every null set is measurable.
          %p
            Given any Cheng space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\mathcal{M})
            %strong completion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mover
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\bar{\mathcal{M}})
            has the same
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying+set"} underlying set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            but a disjoint pair
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,D)
            is
            = succeed "-complemented" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi ℳ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar{\mathcal{M}}
            = succeed "-complemented" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℳ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,B)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⇔
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \Leftrightarrow C
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo ⇔
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \Leftrightarrow D
            are
            = succeed "-full." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℳ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
          %p
            A Cheng space is complete iff it is its own completion; the completion of any Cheng space is complete. The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+function"} identity function
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is measurable in either direction between
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℳ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\mathcal{M})
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mover
                      %mi ℳ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\bar{\mathcal{M}})
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphic"} isomorphic
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cheng
                    %mi Sp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cheng Sp
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cheng
                  %mi Sp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cheng Sp
            on the complete spaces is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalent
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cheng
                  %mi Sp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cheng Sp
            itself (via its
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inclusion+functor"} inclusion functor
          %p
            When restricted to complete spaces, the definition of measurable function is simpler: any partial function under which the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preimage"} preimage
            of any complemented pair is complemented.
          %h2#measures_on_cheng_spaces Measures on Cheng spaces
          %p
            We will define the notion of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+measure"} positive measure
            on a Cheng space; it’s straightforward to generalise to other sorts of measures as described at
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measure"} measure
          %p
            Given a Cheng space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\mathcal{M})
            %strong positive measure
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℳ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\mathcal{M})
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi μ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℳ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0,\infty]
            such that:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/absolutely+continuous+measure"}> absolute continuity
              \:
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu(A,B) = 0
              if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              is full;
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inclusion-exclusion"}> inclusion-exclusion
              \:
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi μ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∩
                      %mi C
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                      %mo ∪
                      %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo +
                      %mi μ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∪
                      %mi C
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                      %mo ∩
                      %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi μ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo +
                      %mi μ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo ,
                      %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu(A \cap C, B \cup D) + \mu(A \cup C, B \cap D) = \mu(A,B) + \mu(C,D)
            %li
              %span.newWikiWord>
                subadditivity
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/subadditive+function"} ?
              \:
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋂
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≤
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mi i
                    %mi μ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu(\bigcup_i A_i, \bigcap_i B_i) \leq \sum_i \mu(A_i,B_i)
              for an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite+sequence"} infinite sequence
              of complemented pairs.
          %p
            We think of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi μ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu(A,B)
            as the measure of
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
